lines=['# V7: partial backbone fine-tuning and hackathon workflow','', '**The default local scanner remains v3. The latest research weights are evaluated separately.**','', '## Local training','',f'Updated {meta["trainable_parameters"]:,} parameters: the final two DINOv2 transformer blocks, final normalization layer and dense segmentation head. Six epochs on local Apple MPS took {meta["seconds"]:.1f} seconds including frozen-prefix extraction. Earlier blocks stayed frozen. Training used 1,732 FoodSeg103 pixel-labeled images and 526 Nutrition5k ingredient-labeled images; no test data entered training.', '', 'Training combines weighted CE/Tversky, an extra supervised boundary penalty, and weak ingredient-presence MIL. Backbone LR 1e-5, head LR 1e-4, seed 171, gradient clipping and cosine scheduling. The selected epoch minimizes validation loss. A second candidate averages the trained parameters 50/50 with MIL-v6 initialization to reduce drift. Both versions are calibrated on validation only.', '',f'Selected candidate: **{r["selected_model"]}**. Policy: `{json.dumps({k:v for k,v in r["policy"]["refinement"].items() if k in ["mode","rule","fallback"]},sort_keys=True)}`.', '', 'Refinement starts from v6 detections. It can replace, intersect or union the chicken geometry, with a validation-selected empty-mask fallback. Selection requires no loss of v6 validation presence or pixel recall and no increase in false-positive images. Other food masks remain unchanged. If no eligible IoU improvement exists, the policy stays identical to v6.', '', '## Chicken results','', 'All sets below have been seen in previous evaluations and are regression evidence. No fresh claim of beating Gemini is supported.','', '| Segmentation set | Model | IoU | Presence recall | Pixel recall | False-positive images |','|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|']
